    {
      "id": "c888e44a-7d13-4c7f-a9ef-79f644184001",
      "name": "Sticky - Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -256,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 630,
        "content": "## 1) Intake & Validation\n- Webhook receives the expense submission (name/email, vendor, amount, currency, category, description, receipt)\n- Set node normalizes the payload + runs a schema check (`valid`, `validationError`)\n- Missing/invalid fields short-circuit to an explicit **400** — bad input never reaches Odoo"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0c4ec972-4bf4-4425-89e2-0951bce2a645",
      "name": "Sticky - Odoo Lookup & Create",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        592,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 980,
        "height": 395,
        "content": "## 2) Odoo Lookup & Expense Creation\n- Employee matched in `hr.employee` by work email — no match = 404, no orphaned expense created\n- Free-text category best-effort matched (`like`) against `product.product`\n- Expense created in `hr.expense`, linked to employee\n- ⚠️ Field names (`unit_amount`, `payment_mode`) assume a stock Odoo 17 schema — verify against your instance"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fbaf7104-9a5a-4c55-94dd-f4f5ebcc2d55",
      "name": "Sticky - Ack & Approval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1632,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 345,
        "content": "## 3) Immediate Ack + Manager Approval\n- Caller gets an immediate **202** once the expense is recorded — never waits on Slack\n- Slack Send-and-Wait (Decision + optional comment) pauses execution until manager responds or 2-day timeout\n- Expenses over $500 get a bold 🔴 warning prefix instead of a second approval hop"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6d249404-4c2e-4bb9-b69b-6ff6cd8baba1",
      "name": "Sticky - Outcomes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2160,
        -48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 465,
        "content": "## 4) Approve / Reject Outcomes\n- **Approve** → `hr.expense.state = approved` + reimbursement email to employee\n- **Needs Correction** → `state = refused` (description prefixed with manager's comment) + resubmit email\n- Both branches read the decision/comment from the Slack custom-form response"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ec580e60-42d7-478f-a52c-c266dcaf7239",
      "name": "Sticky - Error Handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1072,
        432
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 1840,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## 5) Error Handling\n- Every Odoo/Slack/Gmail call uses `onError: continueErrorOutput`, error output wired — nothing fails silently\n- Pre-response failures (lookups, create) → shared **Respond 500**\n- Post-response failures (Slack, updates, emails) → **Log Async Failure**\n- Production: wire that node to an Error Trigger + separate alert channel"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "overview-sticky-expense",
      "name": "Sticky - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -752,
        -768
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 850,
        "content": "## Submit and approve employee expenses in Odoo via webhook and Slack\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow accepts an expense submission over a webhook, validates and normalizes the payload, and returns a 400 response for anything malformed. It looks up the submitting employee and the expense category in Odoo, creates the expense record, and immediately acknowledges the submission with a 202 response. It then asks the employee's manager to approve or reject the expense in Slack; based on the manager's reply it updates the Odoo expense record and emails the employee to confirm approval or explain what needs to be corrected.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Add an Odoo API credential with access to hr.employee, hr.expense, and hr.expense categories.\n- Add a Slack credential and configure the manager-approval Send-and-Wait message/channel.\n- Add a Gmail credential and update the approval/rejection email templates.\n- Point your expense-submission form or app at the webhook URL and match its payload fields to the validation step.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the required fields in the validation step, the expense category lookup logic, or swap the Slack approval for an email- or form-based approval flow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
